{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966796,"nonce":"t1Oaxqgx/H8hoJEduZdMxyxLhVY=","title":"Merging canvas-overlay and dynamic-batch primitives into one composite_frame SDF dispatch","message":"Symptom: cn::popover content, multi-select toolbar bg, focused cn::input fill + outline draw with a horizontal \"split\" — the half overlapping the canvas region shows canvas/page bg through, the half outside the canvas region renders correctly. Only reproduces over a canvas (node_editor_demo); cn_demo never shows it.\n\nCause: composite_frame's single SDF dispatch sorted canvas-emitted primitives + cached_dynamic_batch primitives in one bucket. Z-ordering depended on .stack_layer() reliably bumping the OverlayStack subtree's z above every canvas-emitted z. Anything inside user_ui that pushed z \u003e= overlay-stack-z (e.g. an inner stack_layer from canvas-kit) caused canvas content to overdraw the popover in the merged pass.\n\nFix (commit 9e66a3ab, user-verified 2026-06-13): dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay runs as its own render_primitives_overlay pass on top of composite_frame's canvas-overlay pass. Layering becomes structural rather than z-policy-dependent.\n\n**Why:** verified via wf_cfb5473b-59c — the \"canvas clip leaks into overlay primitives\" hypothesis was structurally impossible (collect_canvas_overlay and collect_dynamic_region_primitives each own a fresh GpuPaintContext with its own clip_stack). The real failure mode was z-interleaving in the merged SDF pass.\n\n**How to apply:** any future code that wants to dispatch a new class of primitives that semantically lives ABOVE canvas content needs its own pass (matching render_foreground_overlay / dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay) — do NOT merge into composite_frame's call. Aux_data must be re-uploaded before each new pass because composite_frame just wrote the canvas overlay's aux to the shared GPU buffer.\n\nRelated: gotcha canvas vs static z ordering — the static-cache vs canvas-overlay version of the same z-layering class.","files":null}]}